{%- comment -%}
  Per-language / per-market product image replacement — the SERVER-SIDE half
  (the storefront swap in the gallery is assets/localized-media.js).

  Prints the replacement image URL for `src` in the visitor's language and
  market, sized to `width`, or NOTHING when there is no replacement — so a
  caller writes:

    {%- capture lm -%}{%- render 'cp-localized-image', src: img_url, width: 1200 -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- if lm != blank -%}{%- assign img_url = lm -%}{%- endif -%}

  The map is `custom.localized_media` (json), written ONLY by the app
  (app/services/localized-media/*): { "v": 1, "e": [ { "o": original filename,
  "l": locale (lowercase), "k": market numeric id or "" for every market,
  "u": replacement CDN url } ] }. Matching is by FILENAME rather than by id:
  `product.images` yields image ids and `product.media` media ids, the two are
  different numbers for the same picture, and the filename is the one key both
  (and the rendered <img> the JS half rewrites) carry.

  Precedence: an entry for the visitor's market beats the all-markets entry of
  the same language; no entry leaves the original untouched.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign h = ''
  assign fn = src | split: '?' | first | split: '/' | last
  assign loc = request.locale.iso_code | downcase
  assign mk = localization.market.id | append: ''
  for e in product.metafields.custom.localized_media.value.e
    if e.o == fn and e.l == loc and e.x == blank
      if e.k == mk
        assign h = e.u
        break
      elsif e.k == blank
        assign h = e.u
      endif
    endif
  endfor
  if h != ''
    if h contains '?'
      echo h | append: '&width=' | append: width
    else
      echo h | append: '?width=' | append: width
    endif
  endif
-%}
